+# Test Design: STORY-640 — Competitor Set Maintenance
+
+## Phase 7 Summary
+
+| Field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Story | STORY-640 |
+| Phase | 7 — Test Design |
+| Status | RED ✓ (29 failed, 0 errors, 0 skipped) |
+| Test file | `tests/test_bsr/test_competitor_set_api.py` |
+| Run command | `TESTING=1 BSR_DASHBOARD_ENABLED=true pytest tests/test_bsr/test_competitor_set_api.py -v --timeout=15` |
+| RED cause | `create_competitor_set_router` not yet present in `src/api/bsr_dashboard.py` |
+
+## Acceptance Criteria Coverage
+
+All 10 TCs from seed §4 are covered. Required function names (seed §3 Acceptance Diff) are present:
+
+| Required name | Test class | Covered |
+|---|---|---|
+| `test_post_competitor` | `TestPostCompetitor` | ✓ |
+| `test_delete_competitor` | `TestDeleteCompetitor` | ✓ |
+| `test_bulk_idempotent` | `TestBulkIdempotent` | ✓ |
+| `test_max_per_asin_enforced` | `TestMaxPerAsin` | ✓ |
+
+## Test Structure
+
+### TC-1 — GET Filter: `TestGetFilter` (3 tests)
+
+| Test | Assertion | Why RED |
+|---|---|---|
+| `test_get_filter_by_asin_returns_only_matching_rows` | 200, `len(rows)==2`, all rows have `our_asin==X` | Factory absent |
+| `test_get_without_filter_returns_all_rows` | 200, `len(rows)==2` | Factory absent |
+| `test_get_filter_no_rows_returns_empty_list` | 200, `rows==[]` | Factory absent |
+
+Cross-ASIN isolation: the session mock returns only rows for the requested `our_asin`. The test verifies
+that no rows for a different ASIN bleed through.
+
+### TC-2 — POST Happy Path: `TestPostCompetitor` (3 tests)
+
+| Test | Assertion | Mock |
+|---|---|---|
+| `test_post_competitor` | 201, `id==42`, `our_asin` and `competitor_asin` in body | `count=0 → INSERT → row` |
+| `test_post_competitor_writes_audit_log` | `audit.log_mutation` called once with `competitor_map.create` | Audit mock |
+| `test_post_competitor_visible_in_get` | POST→201, GET→row id=99 in rows | 3-step side_effect |
+
+Audit assertion checks `"competitor_map.create"` in the stringified call args to remain agnostic
+to whether the operation is passed as positional or keyword argument.
+
+### TC-3 — POST Duplicate: `TestPostDuplicate` (2 tests)
+
+| Test | Assertion | Mock |
+|---|---|---|
+| `test_post_duplicate_returns_409` | 409 | Session raises `IntegrityError` (graceful fallback to `Exception`) |
+| `test_post_duplicate_no_second_audit_row` | `audit.log_mutation` NOT called | Same + audit mock |
+
+`IntegrityError` is imported from `sqlalchemy.exc` with a fallback to a plain `Exception` so the
+test can run even if SQLAlchemy is not installed (it is, but belt-and-suspenders).
+
+### TC-4 — DELETE: `TestDeleteCompetitor` (4 tests)
+
+| Test | Assertion | Mock |
+|---|---|---|
+| `test_delete_competitor` | 204 | `fetch=row → delete=1` |
+| `test_delete_competitor_not_found_returns_404` | 404 | `fetch=[]` (empty result) |
+| `test_delete_competitor_writes_audit_log` | `audit.log_mutation` called with `competitor_map.delete` | Audit mock |
+| `test_delete_competitor_row_gone_from_get` | DELETE→204, GET→id not in rows | 3-step side_effect |
+
+### TC-5 — ASIN Validation: `TestAsinValidation` (3 tests)
+
+| Test | Assertion |
+|---|---|
+| `test_invalid_competitor_asin_returns_422` | 422 for `competitor_asin="INVALID"` |
+| `test_invalid_our_asin_returns_422` | 422 for `our_asin="notvalid"` |
+| `test_valid_asin_format_passes_validation` | 201 for `B0OURRR1234` / `B0COMP11111` |
+
+ASIN regex: `^B0[A-Z0-9]{8}$` (10 chars, starts with B0, rest alphanumeric uppercase).
+
+### TC-6 — Bulk Idempotent: `TestBulkIdempotent` (2 tests)
+
+| Test | Assertion | Mock |
+|---|---|---|
+| `test_bulk_idempotent` | `inserted==3`, `skipped==[asin4, asin5]` | Session with duplicates |
+| `test_bulk_all_new_returns_correct_counts` | `inserted==3`, `skipped==[]` | Clean session |
+
+The bulk endpoint (`POST /bsr/competitors/bulk`) receives `{"competitor_asins": [...]}` and
+must return `{"inserted": N, "skipped": [<asin_list>]}`. Skipped entries are the ASINs that
+already existed (unique constraint check or pre-flight query).
+
+**Phase 8 TC-6 fixture correction** (ref: `ANSWER.md`): The original `test_bulk_idempotent`
+mock used `_mock_result_scalar(0)` which could not express "2 existing rows", making the
+`skipped` assertions unreachable. Fixed per Mark's guidance to use a two-step mock chain:
+(1) pre-flight SELECT → `_mock_result_rows([{existing1}, {existing2}])`, (2) bulk INSERT →
+`_mock_result_scalar(3)`. The `test_bulk_all_new` mock was also updated from a single
+`_mock_result_scalar(0)` to `[_mock_result_rows([]), _mock_result_scalar(3)]` so the INSERT
+`session.execute()` call has a valid mock result. ASIN constants were shortened from 11 to
+10 characters to match the seed spec regex `^B0[A-Z0-9]{8}$` (10 chars).
+
+### TC-7 — Max-per-ASIN: `TestMaxPerAsin` (2 tests)
+
+| Test | Assertion | Mock |
+|---|---|---|
+| `test_max_per_asin_enforced` | 409 with `max_competitors_reached` in response | `count=10` |
+| `test_ninth_post_is_still_allowed` | 201 (count=9 is below cap=10) | `count=9 → INSERT` |
+
+The cap (default 10) is read from `app_config["bsr_competitor_max_per_asin"]`. The Phase 8
+implementation uses `count_result = SELECT COUNT(*) WHERE profile_id=X AND our_asin=Y`.
+
+### TC-8 — Permission Gate: `TestPermissionGate` (4 tests)
+
+| Test | Assertion | Mechanism |
+|---|---|---|
+| `test_post_without_permission_returns_403` | 403 | `is_authorized_fn` returns 403 JSONResponse |
+| `test_delete_without_permission_returns_403` | 403 | Same |
+| `test_get_without_auth_token_returns_401` | 401 | No `Authorization` header |
+| `test_post_without_auth_token_returns_401` | 401 | No `Authorization` header |
+
+The factory accepts an injectable `is_authorized_fn(request, token) → JSONResponse | None`.
+In production this calls `_require_page_access(request, token, page_key="bsr_dashboard")`.
+In tests, `_permission_denied()` returns a pre-built 403 JSONResponse.
+
+### TC-9 — Read-Only Mode: `TestReadOnlyMode` (4 tests)
+
+| Test | Assertion | Mechanism |
+|---|---|---|
+| `test_post_in_read_only_mode_returns_403` | 403 | `check_write_fn` returns blocked dict |
+| `test_delete_in_read_only_mode_returns_403` | 403 | Same |
+| `test_bulk_post_in_read_only_mode_returns_403` | 403 | Same |
+| `test_get_works_in_read_only_mode` | 200 | `check_write_fn` not called for GET |
+
+The factory accepts an injectable `check_write_fn(tool_name: str) → dict | None`.
+In production this is `check_write_allowed("competitor_map")` from `src/tools/_write_guard.py`.
+`_writes_blocked()` returns a dict with `status=403` and `code="READ_ONLY_MODE"`.
+
+### TC-10 — Zero Outbound HTTP: `TestZeroOutboundHttp` (2 tests)
+
+| Test | Assertion | Mechanism |
+|---|---|---|
+| `test_zero_outbound_http` | 201, `len(mock_router.calls)==0` | `respx.mock` strict + autouse |
+| `test_get_zero_outbound_http` | 200, `len(mock_router.calls)==0` | Same |
+
+The root autouse fixture `outbound_http_blocked` in `tests/conftest.py` blocks all real
+outbound `httpx.AsyncClient.send` calls for every test. These TC-10 tests add an explicit
+`respx.mock` layer to produce a named, auditable assertion per the CLAUDE.md mandate:
+> *every story that touches write paths MUST include a test asserting zero outbound HTTP*.
+
+## Dependency Injection Contract
+
+Phase 8 must implement `create_competitor_set_router` with this signature:
+
+```python
+def create_competitor_set_router(
+    async_session: Callable,
+    api_key_verifier: Any,
+    *,
+    audit_logger: Any = None,
+    check_write_fn: Callable | None = None,   # default: check_write_allowed("competitor_map")
+    is_authorized_fn: Callable | None = None, # default: _require_page_access(..., page_key="bsr_dashboard")
+    app_config: dict | None = None,           # default: live app_config table
+) -> Router:
+    ...
+```
+
+Routes (all relative, server mounts at `/api`):
+
+| Verb | Path | Guard |
+|---|---|---|
+| `GET` | `/bsr/competitors` | auth only |
+| `POST` | `/bsr/competitors` | auth + permission + write_guard |
+| `POST` | `/bsr/competitors/bulk` | auth + permission + write_guard |
+| `DELETE` | `/bsr/competitors/{id}` | auth + permission + write_guard |
+
+## External API Isolation
+
+This story adds **no external API write paths**. All operations are pure database CRUD against
+`bsr_competitor_map`. The TC-10 tests assert zero outbound HTTP as required by CLAUDE.md §3
+even though no Amazon API calls are expected. The `outbound_http_blocked` autouse fixture
+provides belt-and-suspenders protection at the test infrastructure level.
+
+## RED State Verification
+
+```
+$ TESTING=1 BSR_DASHBOARD_ENABLED=true python3 -m pytest tests/test_bsr/test_competitor_set_api.py -v --timeout=15
+...
+29 failed in 1.01s
+```
+
+All failures are `AssertionError: create_competitor_set_router not found in src.api.bsr_dashboard`.
+No `ERROR` states. No `SKIP` states. Clean RED.
+
+## Phase 8 Checklist
+
+For tests to turn GREEN, Phase 8 must:
+
+1. Add `create_competitor_set_router` to `src/api/bsr_dashboard.py`
+2. Implement `GET /bsr/competitors` with optional `?our_asin=` and `?profile_id=` filters
+3. Implement `POST /bsr/competitors` with:
+   - ASIN regex validation (`^B0[A-Z0-9]{8}$`)
+   - Count check against `app_config["bsr_competitor_max_per_asin"]` (default 10)
+   - `IntegrityError` → 409 on duplicate
+   - `audit_logger.log_mutation(operation="competitor_map.create", ...)`
+   - `check_write_fn("competitor_map")` guard
+4. Implement `POST /bsr/competitors/bulk` with idempotent insert and `skipped` list
+5. Implement `DELETE /bsr/competitors/{id}` with 404 guard and `audit_logger.log_mutation(operation="competitor_map.delete", ...)`
+6. Wire `is_authorized_fn` (defaulting to `bsr_dashboard` page key check) on all routes
+7. Mount the router in `src/server.py` alongside existing BSR routers
