+# Seed: STORY-815 — Fix PR #319 (STORY-640) Showstoppers & High-Priority Bugs
+
+## Overview
+
+| Field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Mode | bug_fix |
+| Scope | Small |
+| Layer | 1 (Data/Tool) |
+| Epic | BSB (Best Seller Badge) |
+| Depends on | STORY-640 Competitor Set Maintenance (PR #319) |
+| Branch | `story-640/story-640` (same branch as original PR) |
+| Phase Path | 1 → 7 → 8 → Done |
+
+## Problem Statement
+
+PR #319 (STORY-640) has four showstopper bugs and three high-priority issues that block merge:
+
+### Showstoppers
+- **S1**: Schema mismatch — `bsr_competitor_map` table has no `profile_id` column, but all endpoints reference it. Need alembic migration to add the column.
+- **S2**: Bulk endpoint never inserts — `POST /bsr/competitors/bulk` does a SELECT to find existing rows but never executes INSERT SQL. Must implement INSERT with ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING.
+- **S3**: Audit log calls wrong signature — code calls `audit_logger.log_mutation(operation=..., our_asin=..., competitor_asin=...)` but real signature is `log_mutation(user_id, operation, profile_id, resource_id, before, after)`.
+- **S4**: Permission gate not wired — `is_authorized_fn` parameter is never passed in `server.py` mount, so `bsr_dashboard` page-key check is bypassed.
+
+### High Priority
+- **H1**: Frontend passes marketplace ID as profileId — `BsrCompetitorEditor profileId={selectedMarketplace}` passes "ATVPDKIKX0DER" (marketplace) instead of actual profile ID.
+- **H2**: Bulk endpoint does not enforce top-N cap per ASIN.
+- **H5**: ASIN regex allows >10 char ASINs (`{7,}` instead of `{8}`).
+
+## Acceptance Criteria
+
+1. Alembic migration 047 adds `profile_id` column to `bsr_competitor_map` and updates unique constraint
+2. Bulk endpoint actually inserts rows using INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
+3. Audit log calls match `log_mutation(user_id, operation, profile_id, resource_id, before, after)`
+4. `is_authorized_fn` is wired with `_require_page_access` in server.py
+5. Frontend passes actual profile ID (not marketplace ID)
+6. Bulk endpoint enforces top-N cap
+7. ASIN regex is exactly 10 chars: `^B0[A-Z0-9]{8}$`
+8. Integration test against real Postgres validates all fixes
